{
  "$comment": "WARP-536 — canonical OTA release service list. Single source of truth for which images publish-release.yml builds/pushes and which entries land in release.json (design schema v1). Contexts/dockerfiles mirror docker/docker-compose.yml build blocks (context is repo-root-relative). WARP-3001: every compose service with a `build:` block must be listed here or in `excluded` (name -> reason); scripts/release/check_services_drift.py fails the PR lane and the publish gate otherwise. Profile-gated services ARE listed: a box pulls every image, recreates only what it runs, and starts a service only when its own COMPOSE_PROFILES enables it. rag-eval is listed because `eval` is in the default Linux COMPOSE_PROFILES, so boxes run it. healthcheck is what the device-side update agent probes after a swap: `http` entries are the service's own auth-exempt liveness endpoint on its container-internal port; `none` means no plain-HTTP health surface (device-identity-svc is a Unix-socket gRPC sidecar; the openwrt AP container is probed at the network layer; gateway serves TLS only; fleet-agent has no HTTP server). OpenWrt FIRMWARE A/B updates are phase 2 (WARP-534 epic exclusion); the openwrt entry here is the in-container AP image only.",
